    "rich_text_qa46F6": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_xWxEnG": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Are Labels So Important for Food & Beverage Products?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_87EPpj": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Attractive and informative food and beverage labels are important for more than just marketing your product and drawing a consumer’s eye. They are also important for:</p><ul><li> <strong>Safety.</strong> Labels provide clear and concise information about important aspects such as ingredients, expiration dates, and FDA compliance standards.</li><li><strong>Transparency.</strong> Food and beverage labels increase transparency by offering extensive and accurate descriptive information about products and potential allergens.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> Quality labels can withstand wear, moisture, and fluctuating temperatures, thus maintaining integrity during and after shipping.</li></ul>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
